    "show_share": true,
    "description": "Two assistant professors at the Aga Khan University's School of Nursing and Midwifery (AKU-SONAM), Shairfa Lalani and Kiran Shaikh, have been awarded the  Canadian Queen Elizabeth II Diamond Jubilee Scholarships: Advanced-Scholars (QES-AS) . Awarded for a year, the scholarship will help the researchers assess pregnancy-specific anxiety, stress and depression in expecting mothers and to study its relationship with epigenetics (study of changes in organisms caused by gene modification) and its effect on preterm births in the country.",
